{
  "_comment": [
    "A one-time proposal for seeding series onto an existing library, authored by",
    "hand rather than resolved from an API — see VIE-52 for why automation was",
    "cancelled. This file describes Paul and Karen's library specifically; it is",
    "data, not code, and it is here so the seeding is reviewable and repeatable.",
    "",
    "TWO TIERS, and the distinction is the whole point:",
    "  readInOrder: true  — one story across several books. Giving a child book 4",
    "                       of these is useless. This is what Karen asked for.",
    "  readInOrder: false — numbered but self-contained. Baby-Sitters Club #43",
    "                       reads fine without #42. Grouping is still useful for",
    "                       completing a set, but it must never warn about gifting.",
    "",
    "totalKnown is left null wherever the series is open-ended or very long.",
    "A wrong total invents missing books that Karen would go shopping for."
  ],

